node_modules/
# office.db and world.db are pure indexes — delete either at any moment and lose
# nothing. dynamic.db is NOT: it is store-canon, and deleting it costs every
# entity position and attachment since the last crossing-save, plus whatever
# speech has not yet been crystallized. `npm run dynamic:rebuild` is the way back.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
office-keys.json
town-clone/
# the world clone the box actually serves from: `WORLD_CLONE`, else
# `office/world-clone`, else `../postmark-world` (src/world.mjs). Its sibling
# `town-clone/` has been ignored since the beginning and this one never was —
# so on the box, and in any dev worktree that reaches its clone through a link,
# an entire second repository sits untracked in `git status` waiting to be
# swept into a commit by `git add -A`.
world-clone/
world-clone-pool/
draft-locks/
server.log
telemetry/access-*.jsonl
voices-log.jsonl*
# the world store's shadow diffs: an operator's soak record, rebuildable by
# running the shadow again (WORLD_STORE_SHADOW=1)
world-shadow-diff.jsonl*
# the world store's window: regenerated at the end of every hydration, ~850 KiB
# each, and rebuildable from world.db at any moment
*.gexf
.probe/
# the subscription endpoint book (world#18 § The subscription). The act log
# carries a FINGERPRINT of each `deliver_to` and never the URL — `acts` is
# exported to a public archive, frozen on write, so a bearer URL in a payload
# would be a credential published permanently. The URL lives here, box-local,
# read by world2/tools/dispatcher.mjs and by nothing else. It is not a store
# table (the law forbids one) and it is not the record: the record is the log,
# and this book is the office procedure the law puts outside itself.
.subscription-endpoints.json
.subscription-endpoints.json.tmp

# the OMC orchestration layer's runtime residue. It is per-operator session
# state — HUD caches and per-session scratch under `.omc/state/` — that the
# office neither reads nor ships. Two files of it were tracked at the top level
# and therefore rode the release train into `/srv/postmark-office/.omc/` on dev
# and prod, where nothing has ever read them (Keemin 2026-09-21, ROLLOVER 25).
# Untracking is what stops the carry: `stage/` is a `git archive` of the tag, so
# a directory the tag does not carry is never in `dirs.txt` and never rsync'd.
# The name is ALSO in the workflow's exclusion list beside telemetry/.github, as
# the second net for the day somebody re-adds it by reflex.
.omc/

# the read-shape eval's run folders: each agent's working directory and MCP config (tools/read-eval/, POS-486)
.read-eval/
